Energy math helper:

```java
private static final long ENERGY_WINDOW_MS = 60_000L;
private static final long ENERGY_BUDGET_LIMIT_MICRO = 300_000_000L;

private record EnergySegment(String segmentId, String assetId, int densityMilli, long startMs, long endMs) {}
private record WindowContribution(String segmentId, String assetId, int densityMilli, long overlapMs, long energyMicro) {}
private record WindowEvaluation(long startMs, long endMs, long energyMicro, List<WindowContribution> contributions) {}

private static WindowEvaluation evaluateMaxWindow(List<EnergySegment> segments) {
    if (segments.isEmpty()) return null;
    TreeSet<Long> candidates = new TreeSet<>();
    for (EnergySegment s : segments) {
        candidates.add(s.startMs());
        candidates.add(s.endMs());
        candidates.add(s.startMs() - ENERGY_WINDOW_MS);
        candidates.add(s.endMs() - ENERGY_WINDOW_MS);
    }
    WindowEvaluation best = null;
    for (long t : candidates) {
        long windowEnd = t + ENERGY_WINDOW_MS;
        long energy = 0;
        List<WindowContribution> contributions = new ArrayList<>();
        for (EnergySegment s : segments) {
            long overlap = Math.min(s.endMs(), windowEnd) - Math.max(s.startMs(), t);
            if (overlap > 0 && s.densityMilli() > 0) {
                long micro = (long) s.densityMilli() * overlap;
                energy += micro;
                contributions.add(new WindowContribution(s.segmentId(), s.assetId(), s.densityMilli(), overlap, micro));
            }
        }
        if (best == null || energy > best.energyMicro()) {
            best = new WindowEvaluation(t, windowEnd, energy, contributions);
        }
    }
    return best;
}
```

Wait: should contributions include zero-density segments? "查询可定位最大区间及各片段贡献" — contributions of segments in the window. Segments with density 0 contribute 0; including them is harmless but noise. I'll include only positive contributions... Actually for evidence completeness, include all overlapping segments with their (possibly zero) energy? Hmm. I'll include all overlapping segments (overlap > 0) regardless of density, so the window composition is fully explained. Energy 0 contributions are explicit. That seems better for "各片段贡献".

Edge: overlap overflow — densityMilli ≤ 10000, overlap ≤ 60000 → micro ≤ 6e8, fits long. Sum over segments in 60s window: total overlap ≤ 60000ms (segments don't overlap), so energy ≤ 10000×60000 = 6e8. Fine.

Energy to BigDecimal: BigDecimal.valueOf(energyMicro, 6) → scale 6. 300 → "300.000000". Jackson serializes BigDecimal 300.000000 as 300.000000. Test can compare via jsonPath with 300.0? jsonPath("$.maxWindow.energy").value(300.0) — JsonPath reads as Double; 300.000000 == 300.0 ✓. For 300.06 check we only need rejection.

Density to BigDecimal: BigDecimal.valueOf(densityMilli, 3) → 5.000. JSON output 5.000. jsonPath value(5.0) ✓.

Register request validation: @Digits(integer=2, fraction=3) allows up to 99.999; @DecimalMax("10") caps at 10. 10.000 has integer part 2 digits ✓. Negative → DecimalMin("0") rejects. What about "0.0005" (4 decimals)? @Digits fraction=3 rejects → 400 ✓.

densityMilli conversion: request.energyDensity().movePointRight(3).intValueExact() — safe given @Digits. But note BigDecimal "5" → scale 0, movePointRight(3) = 5000 ✓. intValueExact on 10000.000 fine.

Structured params hash: 

```java
private String paramsHash(String operation, Object... params) {
    try {
        return sha256(operation + ":" + objectMapper.writeValueAsString(Arrays.asList(params)));
    } catch (JsonProcessingException e) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("幂等参数序列化失败", e);
    }
}
```

Hmm, operation + ":" + json — operation is fixed enum-like constant, no collision issue. JSON array of params is structured. For segments, convert each SegmentInput to List.of(id, assetId, startMs, endMs) — but id may be null; List.of rejects nulls. Use Arrays.asList (allows nulls). Jackson serializes null → null ✓.

For REPLACE_DRAFT: params = channelId, businessDay.toString(), expectedDraftVersion, List<List<Object>> segments.
For PUBLISH: channelId, businessDay, draftVersion, expectedPublishedVersion.
For REVOKE_GRANT: grantId.
For CREATE_OVERRIDE: overrideKey, channelId, assetId, grantId, priority, startMs, endMs.
For CANCEL_OVERRIDE: overrideKey.
For REGISTER_ENERGY: assetId, energyDensity (string "5.001" — use toPlainString for determinism).

Note: existing idempotent tests expect replay behavior unchanged — the hash storage format changes but behavior same. ✓

Controller: add endpoints:
- POST /api/assets/{assetId}/energy-density
- GET /api/channels/{channelId}/energy-budget?businessDay=yyyy-MM-dd (RequestParam String, parse like businessDay path). Use @RequestParam String businessDay + parseBusinessDay.

Now also need repo.findPublicationSegments(publicationId).

PublicationRow gets 3 new fields — mapper update; findLatestPublication SQL add columns.

